      "text": "\"I put the brown paper in my pocket along with the chalks, and possibly other things. I suppose every one must have reﬂected how primeval and how poetical are the things that one carries in one's pocket: the pocket-knife, for instance the type of all human tools, the infant of the sword. Once I planned to write a book of poems entirely about the things in my pocket. But I found it would be too long: and the age of the great epics is past.\" (From G.K. Chesterton's \"A Piece of Chalk\") Based only on the information provided in the above passage, which one of the following statements is true?",
